                    {
                        "sense_id": "2872d30a-1058-37d3-aeee-31ad1fc03dff",
                        "entry_id": "32cf8d57-d5bd-37b7-b7a0-e9d85403fc89",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Backward motion."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "013410c5-c3b3-41c6-b862-c9b47a80cfdb",
                                "sense_id": "2872d30a-1058-37d3-aeee-31ad1fc03dff",
                                "text": "By simple promotion and remotion, assisted by some flexure and extension, the distal spines of each would reach and scratch the substratum and, on remotion, sweep coarse particles posteriorly and dorsally."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "619c4f11-1c40-42a5-b732-040e3a6c8adf",
                                "sense_id": "2872d30a-1058-37d3-aeee-31ad1fc03dff",
                                "text": "In other arthropods, promotion-remotion of the leg is accomplished at other joints. For example, in spiders promotion-remotion occurs at the coxa-trochanter joint, insects utilize the body-coxa joint, and […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9d51ba5c-8a41-3718-a859-fc3f495cd3f2",
                        "entry_id": "32cf8d57-d5bd-37b7-b7a0-e9d85403fc89",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Removal."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "especially",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f792df97-a840-44d4-97a3-ebf4cff3c9b6",
                                "sense_id": "9d51ba5c-8a41-3718-a859-fc3f495cd3f2",
                                "text": "This act persuades me / That this remotion of the Duke and her / Is practice only."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8bf58f7d-c899-445c-9200-96553eb5025d",
                                "sense_id": "9d51ba5c-8a41-3718-a859-fc3f495cd3f2",
                                "text": "A syllogism disjunctive from the enumeration of the parts is that, in which from the remotion of all the parts the remotion of the whole is concluded."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d7bdf8b2-857f-4282-83de-cefc7d78ca40",
                                "sense_id": "9d51ba5c-8a41-3718-a859-fc3f495cd3f2",
                                "text": "We may proceed from the remotion of the consequent to the remotion of the antecedent."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "de8857a5-2aba-4ba1-ae4e-855407ef756e",
                                "sense_id": "9d51ba5c-8a41-3718-a859-fc3f495cd3f2",
                                "text": "The remotion of Cr3+ from the wastewater prevents its possible oxidation."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
